    <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
    <p class="lead" style="margin-top:var(--space-4)">These terms govern the booking of the Palomino Islands tour operated by Ecocruceros. By booking, you accept the conditions described here.</p>
    <p style="color:var(--text-secondary);margin-top:var(--space-2)">Last updated: June 20, 2026.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:var(--space-12)">1. The service</h2>
    <p>Ecocruceros offers a yacht voyage from the private pier in La Punta, Callao, to the Palomino Islands, lasting approximately 3 to 4 hours. Departures are <strong>by reservation</strong>, with no fixed schedule, and are subject to sea conditions and to a minimum/maximum number of passengers.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:var(--space-8)">2. Bookings and payments</h2>
    <p>Bookings are arranged via WhatsApp ({{ site.whatsappDisplay }}) in these steps: (1) you tell us the date and number of passengers; (2) we confirm availability and payment details; (3) you send names, ages, IDs and nationalities; (4) after payment, we send the boarding address.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:var(--space-3)">Booking requests may also be sent to <a href="mailto:reservas@ecocruceros.com">reservas@ecocruceros.com</a>, including each passenger's name, age, ID number and nationality. The service is paid in <strong>full (100%)</strong>, at the latest <strong>24 hours before</strong> departure, and the payment receipt must be emailed to us. For groups, one passenger goes free from 15 passengers onward. Pickup from other districts (San Borja, Barranco, La Molina, etc.) carries an additional charge, subject to prior arrangement.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:var(--space-3)">No online payments are made through this website. Current prices: residents from S/. 179 and visitors from US$69 (see <a href="/en/tour/precios/">pricing</a>). The <strong>SERNANP fee is not included</strong> and is paid separately. Prices may change and are confirmed at the time of booking.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:var(--space-8)">3. Cancellation and weather policy</h2>
    <p>For safety, the tour may be rescheduled or cancelled when sea or weather conditions require it. In that case we will arrange a new date or the appropriate option.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:var(--space-3)">Passengers may cancel a booking up to <strong>24 hours before</strong> the service starts; after that window, the booking is treated as a <strong>no show</strong>. The waiting time to pick up passengers at the agreed point is <strong>15 minutes</strong>; if a passenger cannot be reached, it will be treated as a NO SHOW and a proportional charge of the booking will apply.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:var(--space-8)">4. Insurance</h2>
    <p>All passengers are covered by insurance throughout the voyage.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:var(--space-8)">5. Wildlife and experience</h2>
    <p>Sightings of sea lions, Humboldt penguins and guano birds are guaranteed under normal conditions. <strong>Whale sightings are seasonal and not guaranteed.</strong> The experience may vary depending on sea and weather conditions.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:var(--space-8)">6. Passenger responsibilities</h2>
    <ul style="margin-top:var(--space-2);padding-left:var(--space-6)">
      <li>Follow the crew's instructions at all times.</li>
      <li>Use the indicated safety equipment (life vest mandatory).</li>
      <li>Do not touch or feed wildlife and keep a respectful distance.</li>
      <li>Present the ID documents declared in the booking.</li>
      <li>Arrive on time at the boarding point.</li>
      <li>Check your belongings before the service ends; the company is not responsible for personal items left behind.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="margin-top:var(--space-8)">7. Health and safety</h2>
    <p>Wearing a life vest is mandatory during navigation and swimming. We recommend informing the crew of any relevant health condition before departure.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:var(--space-3)"><strong>No swimming ability required:</strong> you can enter the sea wearing a life vest and accompanied by the crew during the swim stop.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:var(--space-8)">8. Image consent</h2>
    <p>During the tour we may take photographs or videos for promotional purposes. If you prefer not to appear, please let the crew know before departure.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:var(--space-8)">9. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>Ecocruceros shall not be liable for failures arising from force majeure or unforeseeable events (weather conditions, maritime authority directives, etc.), nor for damages caused by a passenger's failure to follow safety instructions.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:var(--space-8)">10. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>The content of this site (text, images, logo and design) belongs to Ecocruceros or its rights holders and may not be reproduced without authorization.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:var(--space-8)">11. Governing law and jurisdiction</h2>
    <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Peru. Any dispute shall be submitted to the jurisdiction of the courts of Callao, Peru.</p>

